ing timeline. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3056":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-43","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"| API                                       | Purpose                                         |\n| ----------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `restoreTravelJournal(snapshot, options)` | Atomically restore an externally owned journal. |","locale":"en","table":"table-5"},"3057":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-44","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#persistence","content":"The exported `Travels` value is the persistence namespace, not a constructor.","locale":"en"},"3058":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-45","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`findStateCompatibilityIssues(value, options?)` inspects durable-data hazards.","locale":"en"},"3059":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-46","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`validateTravelPatches(...)` validates patch structure and retained values.","locale":"en"},"3060":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-47","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`validateTravelHistoryEntry(...)` validates one forward/inverse history entry.","locale":"en"},"3061":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-48","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`assertTravelHistoryEntryRecordable(...)` preflights controlled ingress without changing journal state.","locale":"en"},"3062":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-49","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#validation-helpers","content":"`createPatchableTravels(...)` constrains initial state statically and validates it immediately at runtime.","locale":"en"},"3063":{"id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods-50","page_id":"/docs/reference/instance-methods","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/instance-methods#subscriptions","content":"`subscribe(listener)` returns an unsubscribe function. Events publish after commit; observer failures are isolated through `onObserverError`. Do not synchronously call mutating methods from an observer. See Observers and Events.","locale":"en"},"3064":{"id":"/docs/reference/options","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"page","content":"Configuration Options","breadcrumbs":["Travels","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options","locale":"en"},"3065":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-0","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options","content":"Reference for timeline creation, restore, persistence, patches, hooks, and Mutative options.","locale":"en"},"3066":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-1","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"Timeline options","locale":"en"},"3067":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-2","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"Observer and lifecycle hooks","locale":"en"},"3068":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-3","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"Restore options","locale":"en"},"3069":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-4","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options#serialization-options","content":"Serialization options","locale":"en"},"3070":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-5","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"Deserialization options","locale":"en"},"3071":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-6","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"Capability-specific options","locale":"en"},"3072":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-7","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options","content":"Factory overloads infer archive mode and patch options from the options you provide. The exact generated types are available under `TravelsOptions` and `RestoreTravelsOptions`.","locale":"en"},"3073":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-8","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option       | Type     | Default | Purpose                                                         |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `maxHistory` | `number` | `10`    | Maximum retained patch entries; must be a non-negative integer. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3074":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-9","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option        | Type      | Default | Purpose                                                                              |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `autoArchive` | `boolean` | `true`  | Archive every effective update automatically, or expose manual `archive()` controls. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3075":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-10","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option    | Type      | Default | Purpose                                                                  |\n| --------- | --------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `mutable` | `boolean` | `false` | Apply patches to the live object for identity-sensitive reactive stores. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3076":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-11","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option                   | Type      | Default               | Purpose                                                                   |\n| ------------------------ | --------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `warnOnUnsupportedState` | `boolean` | `true` in development | Enable compatibility diagnostics for state, patches, paths, and metadata. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3077":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-12","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option           | Type            | Default | Purpose                                                                              |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `patchesOptions` | `PatchesOption` | `{}`    | Customize patch representation, including `pathAsArray`; patches cannot be disabled. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3078":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-13","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option             | Type      | Default | Purpose                                                              |\n| ------------------ | --------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `enableAutoFreeze` | `boolean` | `false` | Freeze produced immutable states; incompatible with `mutable: true`. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3079":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-14","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option   | Type                   | Default | Purpose                                          |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | ------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `strict` | Mutative strict option | `false` | Match Mutative’s stricter immutability behavior. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3080":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-15","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"| Option | Type                 | Default          | Purpose                                                         |\n| ------ | -------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mark` | Mutative mark option | Mutative default | Customize which objects Mutative treats as immutable/draftable. |","locale":"en","table":"table-0"},"3081":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-16","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#timeline-options","content":"See the Mutative documentation for the underlying `strict`, `mark`, and auto-freeze semantics. When persisted history was recorded with custom `strict` or `mark`, pass matching values through `replayOptions` during semantic deserialization.","locale":"en"},"3082":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-17","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option     | Signature input      | When it runs                                       |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `devtools` | `TravelsEvent<S, P>` | After each committed event, alongside subscribers. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3083":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-18","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option    | Signature input      | When it runs                                                                                 |\n| --------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onError` | Wrapped core `Error` | When Travels reports a core operation failure; nested transaction errors settle at the root. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3084":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-19","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option            | Signature input           | When it runs                                 |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onBranchDiscard` | `{ position, discarded }` | After a committed edit removes redo entries. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3085":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-20","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option      | Signature input     | When it runs                                                                |\n| ----------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onWarning` | `{ code, message }` | For non-fatal normalization, compatibility, position, and history warnings. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3086":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-21","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"| Option            | Signature input     | When it runs                                                      |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onObserverError` | `{ source, error }` | When a listener or lifecycle/diagnostic hook throws after commit. |","locale":"en","table":"table-1"},"3087":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-22","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#observer-and-lifecycle-hooks","content":"Observer errors do not roll back committed transitions. Hook functions should not synchronously mutate the same timeline.","locale":"en"},"3088":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-23","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"`restoreTravels(snapshot, options?)` accepts applicable creation options but deliberately does not accept a separate `initialState` or `history`; the complete snapshot is the atomic state/history input.","locale":"en"},"3089":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-24","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"For mutable integration, it additionally accepts:","locale":"en"},"3090":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-25","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#restore-options","content":"`target` must be a compatible object or array root and requires `mutable: true`. Travels overwrites it in place with detached snapshot state. `restoreTravelJournal(snapshot, { apply, ...options })` instead requires the external owner’s synchronous navigation callback and does not expose state-owning mutable options.","locale":"en"},"3091":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-26","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#serialization-options","content":"`strict` rejects any current state, retained patch value/path, or metadata that cannot round-trip through the documented JSON persistence contract. Use `assertPersistenceCompatible()` when validation should happen without creating a snapshot.","locale":"en"},"3092":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-27","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option       | Purpose                                                                                      |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `validation` | `'structural'` by default; `'semantic'` additionally replays and reverses reachable entries. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3093":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-28","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option     | Purpose                                                                                   |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fallback` | A snapshot or synchronous factory used after detected parse/migration/validation failure. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3094":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-29","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option    | Purpose                                                                          |\n| --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `migrate` | A synchronous callback that converts old input into the current snapshot schema. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3095":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-30","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option    | Purpose                                                      |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onError` | Receives `TravelsPersistenceError` before fallback or throw. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3096":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-31","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"| Option          | Purpose                                                             |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `replayOptions` | Matching Mutative `strict` and `mark` settings for semantic replay. |","locale":"en","table":"table-2"},"3097":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-32","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#deserialization-options","content":"All storage, network, decompression, and application-envelope verification work belongs before the synchronous deserialization call.","locale":"en"},"3098":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-33","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"`createTravels()` owns updates and supports `mutable`, tracking, transactions, and controls.","locale":"en"},"3099":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-34","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"`createPatchableTravels()` accepts the durable state contract and validates initial state immediately.","locale":"en"},"3100":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-35","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options","content":"`createTravelJournal()` requires `apply` and rejects state-owning `mutable` options.","locale":"en"},"3101":{"id":"/docs/reference/options-36","page_id":"/docs/reference/options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/reference/options#capability-specific-options"