-- |\n| Many documents, indexes, cleanup queries | Dexie.js            |"],[2946,"| Requirement                       | Recommended adapter       |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| One snapshot per app, minimal API | localForage or localspace |"],[2950,"| Requirement                   | Recommended adapter                                                          |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Existing localForage codebase | localForage first; localspace when adopting TypeScript-first APIs or batches |"],[2137,"| Scenario                                            | Recommended approach                                           |\n| --------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Collaborative conflict merging and concurrent users | A CRDT/OT system; Travels does not resolve conflicts by itself |"],[2135,"| Scenario                                       | Recommended approach                                             |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tiny state and a handful of local-only entries | A snapshot stack, Redux-undo, or Zundo may be simpler and faster |"],[2134,"| Scenario                                   | Recommended approach                                          |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Replayable operation logs or undo metadata | Travels: entries contain forward/inverse patches and metadata |"],[2136,"| Scenario                                | Recommended approach                                        |\n| --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Replace most or all state on every edit | Measure both approaches; patches can approach snapshot cost |"],[2133,"| Scenario                               | Recommended approach                                       |\n| -------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Long history that must survive reloads | Travels: one versioned snapshot includes state and history |"],[2132,"| Scenario                         | Recommended approach                                               |\n| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Large state with localized edits | Travels: retained patches usually avoid repeated full-state copies |"],[2963,"| Scenario                     | Host-application responsibility                                                                                                            |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| Multi-device synchronization | Bind document and tenant/user identity to a server-controlled revision, and resolve stale or conflicting snapshots before deserialization. |"],[2860,"| Scenario                     | Host-application responsibility                                                                            |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Multi-device synchronization | Bind tenant/user/document identity to a server-controlled revision and resolve stale/conflicting snapshots |"],[2858,"| Scenario                  | Host-application responsibility                               |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Ephemeral local undo/redo | Replay validation and a safe fallback are normally sufficient |"],[2962,"| Scenario                 | Host-application responsibility                                                                                                                                                                      |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Important offline drafts | Checksum the exact encoded bytes, store a monotonic revision, and retain at least one previously verified generation. A checksum detects accidental corruption; it does not authenticate the writer. |"],[2964,"| Scenario                 | Host-application responsibility                                                                                                                               |\n| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tamper-resistant storage | Verify a server-held HMAC, digital signature, or authenticated-encryption tag. A key stored beside attacker-controlled browser data does not establish trust. |"],[2859,"| Scenario                 | Host-application responsibility                                                          |\n| ------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Important offline drafts | Checksum exact bytes, keep a monotonic revision, retain a previously verified generation |"],[2861,"| Scenario                 | Host-application responsibility                                       |\n| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Tamper-resistant storage | Verify a server-held HMAC, signature, or authenticated-encryption tag |"],[2961,"| Scenario               | Host-application responsibility                