"Detecting History Overflow"],[2236,"Detecting History Overflow"],[2120,"Development builds scan initial and changed state plus retained patches and metadata for known hazards. `warnOnUnsupportedState: false` controls those warnings; it does not enable Map/Set or make invalid persistence safe. `onWarning` receives structured warning codes, and `onObserverError` isolates failures thrown by diagnostic or notification hooks."],[2095,"Development diagnostics"],[3135,"Development Setup"],[2467,"Devtools"],[5745,"Devtools"],[5771,"Devtools 遵循与订阅者相同的提交后、共享视图和错误隔离规则。请保持 devtools 的工作轻量，避免同步修改时间线，并复制需要比事件存活更久的数据。"],[2493,"Devtools follows the same post-commit, shared-view, and error-isolation rules as a subscriber. Keep devtools work light, avoid synchronous timeline mutations, and copy data that must outlive the event."],[1867,"devtools()?"],[5145,"devtools()?"],[6190,"Dexie 专属说明："],[2912,"Dexie-specific notes:"],[2881,"Dexie.js"],[2891,"Dexie.js"],[6159,"Dexie.js"],[6169,"Dexie.js"],[6185,"Dexie.js 是 IndexedDB 的高层封装，提供表 API、模式版本管理、索引、事务和批量操作。当应用需要保存许多条持久化时间线，并按文档、时间戳、所有者或项目查询时，它很合适。"],[6255,"Dexie.js 文档：https://dexie.org/docs/index"],[6256,"Dexie.js API 参考：https://dexie.org/docs/API-Reference"],[2978,"Dexie.js API reference: https://dexie.org/docs/API-Reference"],[2977,"Dexie.js documentation: https://dexie.org/docs/index"],[2907,"Dexie.js is a high-level IndexedDB wrapper with table APIs, schema versioning, indexes, transactions, and bulk operations. It is a good fit when an app stores many persisted timelines and needs to query them by document, timestamp, owner, or project."],[3226,"Diagnose common update, navigation, persistence, mutable-mode, and integration problems."],[2691,"Direct core integration"],[2545,"Direct replacement"],[93,"direction?"],[100,"direction?"],[3370,"direction?"],[3377,"direction?"],[1693,"discarded"],[4971,"discarded"],[2668,"Do not call `createTravels()` unconditionally on every render. Treat `initialState` as initialization input; to load a different document, explicitly replace state or create a new keyed editor owner rather than silently resetting history during render."],[2672,"Do not call `setState()`, `back()`, or other timeline mutations during render or synchronously from a Travels observer. Event handlers and appropriately scheduled effects/tasks keep transitions ordered."],[3265,"Do not combine mutable mode with `enableAutoFreeze`. Read the complete operation identity table."],[3251,"Do not create a new timeline on every component render."],[2656,"Do not enable `enableAutoFreeze` with mutable mode. Map and Set remain unsupported even when MobX or Vue can observe them; normalize collections before passing them to Travels."],[2154,"Do not feed delegated navigation back into `recordPatches()`."],[2699,"Do not let an action write independently to both stores in a way that creates divergent states. Either route updates through Travels and mirror its committed state, or keep Zustand authoritative and use the official binding or a controlled journal."],[2530,"Do not pass an async function or return a Promise from the callback. Await network and storage work before starting the transaction:"],[3260,"Do not pass separate `history`, `initialPatches`, or `initialPosition` options in v3. Pass one complete snapshot to `restoreTravels()`."],[3271,"Do not record navigation triggered by `apply` as a new edit."],[2846,"Do not replay old Map/Set-specific patch histories after normalizing current state. Reference-based collection paths and values cannot be migrated reliably as generic JSON Patch. Materialize the authoritative current state outside Travels, convert it to supported plain objects and dense arrays, then create a new history baseline."],[2777,"Do not replay old patch history generated from Map/Set mutations. Such history can contain collection-specific values or non-JSON path locators whose reference identity cannot be migrated reliably. Decode the legacy record outside Travels, materialize its authori