历史。"],[5592,"Travels 保证每次 Journal 变更在内部都是原子的：格式错误、为空或只有单向的补丁对、不安全路径、不支持的补丁/状态值、元数据克隆失败以及受控导航失败，都不会部分改变 Journal 状态或历史记录。受控补丁入口采用与持久化历史相同的结构归一化，并同样保证访问器安全。"],[5793,"Travels 不会合并并发编辑，也不会消解冲突。在替换或变基本地状态之前，先确定文档标识、修订号顺序和冲突处理方式。当历史记录的来源很重要时，应在反序列化或替换之前，在 Travels 之外校验远程快照。参见安全与完整性。"],[6144,"Travels 不是 CRDT 或操作转换系统，不会合并并发历史记录，也不会解决冲突编辑。同步层必须明确以下事项："],[6053,"Travels 不再支持在不可变状态或可变状态中使用 Map 或 Set。初始状态与更新会立即失败，恢复的状态或补丁载荷若包含集合，也会在结构校验阶段被拒绝。请在创建或更新 Travels 实例之前先把集合规范化："],[5873,"Travels 采用 MIT 许可，使用 TypeScript 编写。你可以在文档的示例页面找到可运行示例，或浏览 GitHub 仓库。官方绑定包括 React 的 use-travel 和 Zustand 的 zustand-travel。"],[6068,"Travels 的持久化不依赖具体存储。`serialize()` 返回一个带版本号的快照；如何编码和存储，由你的应用决定。恢复始终只走一条路径：先用 `Travels.deserialize()` 解码，再把完整结果传给 `restoreTravels()` 或 `restoreTravelJournal()`。"],[6167,"Travels 的持久化不依赖具体存储。唯一需要存储的值，就是 `travels.serialize()` 返回的带版本号快照。用 `Travels.deserialize(...)` 恢复它，再把校验后的快照传给 `restoreTravels(...)`。"],[5374,"Travels 的持久化契约有意比 JavaScript 的对象模型更小。它不仅适用于当前状态，也适用于旧补丁中保留的值、补丁路径以及自定义历史元数据，而不只是传给 `createTravels()` 的那个对象。"],[5898,"Travels 的核心不依赖任何 UI 框架。合适的集成方式取决于状态由谁掌管，以及你的响应式系统需要的是新引用还是稳定的对象身份。"],[5569,"Travels 分离补丁对与元数据，更新游标和保留的历史记录，然后发布一个 `recordPatches` 事件。"],[6078,"Travels 会把快照状态和时间线当作一个原子输入整体接收。后续导航中补丁如何提交，仍由所有者决定。"],[6544,"Travels 会回滚通过自身 API 完成的写入。它无法回滚对可变 Store 的直接赋值、网络请求、DOM 变更、存储写入或其他外部副作用。"],[5479,"Travels 会提交一个不可变状态，保存正向与反向补丁，推进游标，并通知订阅者。元数据会附加到历史条目上，并包含在持久化快照中。"],[6553,"Travels 会校验补丁结构，但有意不重新生成补丁来证明所有者的转换。这一对应关系由适配器负责。"],[6017,"Travels 会用快照状态就地覆盖 `target`，因此 Store 不再需要预先填入与恢复后历史一致的数据。"],[5604,"Travels 将操作错误、持久化解码错误、非致命警告和观察者失败区分开来。应匹配稳定的 `code` 值，而不是生产环境中的错误消息文本。"],[6496,"Travels 结合了基于示例的测试、基于属性的测试、浏览器测试、包使用方测试、覆盖率测试与变异冒烟测试。"],[5361,"Travels 历史模式版本。"],[6276,"Travels 面向支持所需标准 JavaScript 与 JSON API 的现代浏览器。持久化示例会在环境支持时使用 `localStorage`、IndexedDB 与 BroadcastChannel。"],[5327,"Travels 如何工作"],[5304,"Travels 时间线中有两个相关但不同的概念：导航使用的**保留历史窗口**，以及 `reset()` 使用的**实例基线**。理解它们的生命周期，可以避免许多微妙的撤销/重做缺陷。"],[6389,"Travels 使用 TypeScript 编写，并为 ESM 与 CommonJS 使用方提供声明文件。大多数应用可以依赖工厂函数的类型推断，而不必逐个写出泛型参数。"],[5849,"Travels 是一个与框架无关的状态历史引擎，为应用提供可靠的撤销/重做能力。它记录正向与反向 JSON Patch，因此状态庞大、编辑频繁而细微的应用也能保留紧凑的时间线，将其持久化，并在之后恢复。"],[5456,"Travels 提供 ESM、CommonJS、UMD 与 TypeScript 声明文件。运行时支持策略见兼容性。"],[5409,"Travels 围绕一个明确的取舍而设计：把一部分计算花在生成与应用补丁上，以缩小保留历史、让完整时间线的持久化变得可行。它并不打算在每一项更新延迟基准上都胜出。"],[5842,"Travels 文档"],[5686,"Travels 在记录任何内容之前，会先用 `snapshot.state` 的副本就地覆盖 `target`，因此实时对象与恢复后的补丁历史总是从同一份数据开始。快照本身永远不会被修改。`target` 要求 `mutable: true`，并且其根类型（普通对象或数组）必须与快照状态一致；两个根都不得含有自有 `__proto__` 键，不满足时会以 `INVALID_OPTION` 拒绝。"],[6271,"Travels 在以下环境经过测试："],[5859,"Travels 针对历史体积、持久化和可重放的操作日志进行了优化。它尤其适合可视化编辑器、表单搭建器、本地优先应用、工作流设计器，以及其他需要让用户安全探索的编辑场景。"],[6285,"Travels 遵循 semver："],[3218,"Travels combines example-based, property-based, browser, package-consumer, coverage, and mutation smoke tests."],[2201,"Travels commits one immutable state, stores forward and inverse patches, advances the cursor, and notifies subscribers. Metadata is attached to the history entry and included in persistence snapshots."],[2291,"Travels detaches the patch pair and metadata, updates its cursor and retained history, then publishes one `recordPatches` event."],[2564,"Travels Documentation"],[2515,"Travels does not merge concurrent edits or resolve conflicts. Decide document identity, revision ordering, and conflict handling before replacing or rebasing local state. When history provenance matters, verify the remote snapshot outside Travels before deserialization or replacement. See Security and Integrity."],[3007,"Travels follows semver:"],[2571,"Travels is a framework-agnostic state history engine for durable undo/redo. It records forward and inverse JSON Patches, so applications with large state and small, frequent edits can retain compact timelines, persist them, and restore them later."],[2131,"Travels is designed around a specific trade-off: spend work generating and applying patches to reduce retained history size and make complete timelines practical to persist. It is not intended to win every update-latency benchmark."],[2159,"Travels is likely a strong fit when most answers are yes:"],[2595,"Travels is MIT licensed and written in TypeScript. Find runnable examples in the documentation’s Examples page, or browse the GitHub repository. The official bindings are use-travel for React and zustand-travel for Zustand."],[2866,"Travels is not a CRDT or operational-transform system. It does not merge concurrent histories or resolve conflicting edits. A synchronization layer must define:"],[2581,"Travels is optimized for history size, persistence, and replayable operation logs. It is especially useful for visual editors, form builders, local-first applications, workflow designers, and other editing experiences where users need a safe way to explore."],[2993,"Travels is tested on:"],[3111,"Travels is written in TypeScript and ships declarations for both ESM and CommonJS consumers. Most applications can rely on factory inference rather than spelling every generic."],[2314,"Travels makes each journal mutation internally atomic: malformed, empty, or one-sided patch pairs, unsafe paths, unsupported patch/state values, metadata cloning failures, and controlled navigation failures do not partially change journal state or history. Controlled patch ingress uses the same accessor-safe structural normalization as persisted history."],[2775,"Travels no longer supports Map or Set in either immutable or mutable state. Initial state and updates fail fast, and restored state or patch payloads containing collections are rejected during structural validation. Normalize collections before creating or updating a Travels instance:"],[2408,"Travels overwrites `target` in place with a copy of `snapshot.state` before it records anything, so the live object and the restored patch history always start from the same data. The snapshot itself is never mutated. `target` requires `mutable: true` and must have the same root kind (plain object or array) as the snapshot state, and neither root may have an own `__proto__` key; it is rejected with `INVALID_OPTION` otherwise."],[2739,"Travels overwrites `target` in place with the snapshot state, so the store no longer has to be pre-populated to match the restored history."],[2790,"Travels persistence is storage-agnostic. `serialize()` returns one versioned snapshot; your application chooses how to encode and store it. Restore always follows one path: decode with `Travels.deserialize()`, then pass the complete result to `restoreTravels()` or `restoreTravelJournal()`."],[2889,"Travels persistence is storage-agnostic. The only value that needs to be stored is the versioned snapshot returned by `travels.serialize()`. Restore it with `Travels.deserialize(...)`, then pass the validated snapshot to `restoreTravels(...)`."],[3266,"Travels rolls back writes made through its own APIs. It cannot roll back direct mutable-store assignments, network requests, DOM changes, storage writes, or other external side effects."],[2326,"Travels separates operation errors, persistence decoding errors, non-fatal warnings, and observer failures. Match stable `code` values rather than production error message text."],[2178,"Travels ships ESM, CommonJS, UMD, and TypeScript declarations. The runtime support policy is documented under Compatibility."],[2998,"Travels targets modern browsers that support the required standard JavaScript and JSON APIs. Persistence examples use `localStorage`, IndexedDB, and BroadcastChannel when available."],[2059,"Travels turns each effective update into an immutable state transition plus two patch groups: one that moves forward and one that restores the previous state. The retained sequence of those transitions is the history."],[3275,"Travels validates patch structure but deliberately does not regenerate patches to prove the owner’s transition. That relationship belongs to the adapter."],[2620,"Travels’ core does not depend on a UI framework. The right integration depends on who owns state and whether your reactive system expects a new reference or stable object identity."],[2096,"Travels’ durable contract is deliberately smaller than JavaScript’s object model. It applies to current state, values retained in old patches, patch paths, and custom history metadata—not just the object passed to `createTravels()`."],[2008,"TRAVELS\\_HISTORY\\_SCHEMA\\_VERSION"],[5286,"TRAVELS\\_HISTORY\\_SCHEMA\\_VERSION"],[1498,"Travels<S, _F, A, P>"],[4776,"Travels<S, _F, A, P>"],[1688,"TravelsBranchDiscardEvent<P>"],[4966,"TravelsBranchDiscardEvent<P>"],[1702,"TravelsControlledApply()<S, P>"],[4980,"TravelsControlledApply()<S, P>"],[1717,"TravelsControlledTransition<S, P>"],[4995,"TravelsControlledTransition<S, P>"],[1195,"TravelsControls<S, P>"],[4473,"TravelsControls<S, P>"],[1746,"TravelsDeserializeOptions<S, P>"],[5024,"TravelsDeserializeOptions<S, P>"],[1,"TravelsError"],[3278,"TravelsError"],[1781,"TravelsErrorCode"],[5059,"TravelsErrorCode"],[1785,"TravelsEvent<S, P>"],[5063,"TravelsEvent<S, P>"],[1818,"TravelsEventType"],[5096,"TravelsEventType"],[1823,"TravelsHistoryValidationMode"],[5101,"TravelsHistoryValidationMode"],[1827,"TravelsKnownEventType"],[5105,"TravelsKnownEventType"],[1834,"TravelsMigration()<S, P>"],[5112,"TravelsMigration()<S, P>"],[1848,"TravelsObserverErrorEvent"],[5126,"TravelsObserverErrorEvent"],[1859,"TravelsObserverErrorSource"],[5137,"TravelsObserverErrorSource"],[1863,"TravelsOptions<F, A, P, S>"],[5141,"TravelsOptions<F, A, P, S>"],[83,"TravelsPersistenceError"],[3360,"TravelsPersistenceError"],[1935,"TravelsPersistenceErrorCode"],[5213,"TravelsPersistenceErrorCode"],[1939,"TravelsReplayOptions"],[5217,"TravelsReplayOptions"],[1961,"TravelsSerializedHistory<S, P>"],[5239,"TravelsSerializedHistory<S, P>"],[1952,"TravelsSerializeOptions"],[5230,"TravelsSerializeOptions"],[175,"TravelsTypeError"],[3452,"TravelsTypeError"],[1986,"TravelsWarning"],[5264,"TravelsWarning"],[1997,"TravelsWarningCode"],[5275,"TravelsWarningCode"],[2707,"Treat shared views as read-only"],[2262,"t