ion succeeds and publishes one `go` event, advancing `getRevision()` once, in both immutable and mutable mode. Listeners that persisted only on `archive` should persist on every committed event:"],[2073,"With `autoArchive: true`, every effective `setState()` creates an entry. With `autoArchive: false`, state updates remain pending until `archive()` or an operation that implicitly archives them."],[2071,"With `mutable: true`, Travels applies patches back to the original object so MobX, Vue, Pinia, or custom proxies can keep observing the same reference. It still generates forward and inverse patches for navigation and persistence."],[2139,"With Travels, immutable updates also use Mutative’s structural sharing. “Patch-based” does not mean every retained state is deep-cloned, and “smaller history” does not imply the lowest possible `setState()` latency."],[2353,"Without the hook, warnings are written to the console only in development. Disabling compatibility warnings does not disable runtime correctness checks."],[2163,"Would a versioned snapshot simplify local-first storage?"],[2242,"Wrap `setState` to inject metadata like timestamps or user IDs into the state. To label the history entry instead, add your fields to the `metadata` argument the wrapper forwards, which `getMetadata()` returns for each entry."],[2244,"Wrap methods to control how frequently they can be called:"],[2243,"Wrap methods to record all operations before and after execution:"],[2241,"Wrap methods to verify permissions before allowing execution:"],[2572,"Write updates with familiar mutation syntax. Travels uses Mutative to produce immutable state by default, while mutable mode and controlled journals support reactive stores and externally owned state."],[2399,"You batch updates with `autoArchive: false` but still expect the live store reference to update immediately."],[2202,"You can also provide a direct value or return a new state. Updaters must be synchronous:"],[3112,"You can also provide an e